  "universes": 1,
  "notes": "<div><font size=\"5\"><b>Sounds</b></font></div><div>A stormy night in sound and light: rain, wind and thunder, a church bell, applause and a short piece of music. The sounds were made for this example from noise and tones alone, so they are free to use.</div><div><b><font color=\"#ffb020\">What is in it</font></b></div><ul><li>Sounds 1 to 8 on the <b>Sounds</b> view, music in cyan and sound effects in pink. 1 is the music; 2 (Rain) and 3 (Wind) go round in a loop; 4 and 5 are the same thunder, near and far (lower, quieter, at the right, with more reverb); 6 is a church bell with an echo; 7 is applause; 8 is the music of 1 played slower, at the same pitch.</li><li>Memories 1 to 4 light the stage of example 3: Night, Storm, Church and Morning. Effect 1 flickers the front lights white: lightning.</li><li>The files lie in the folder \"8 Sounds sounds\" beside the project. A project with sounds gets such a folder when it is saved.</li></ul><div><b><font color=\"#ffb020\">Try it</font></b></div><ol><li>Open <b>Sounds</b>. The key of a sound brings its fader up in the sound's fade-in time, which starts it, and down in its fade-out time, which stops it. The fader itself sets how loud it plays, up to the sound's own volume.</li><li>Start Rain (2) and Wind (3): they play until their keys take them down. The name under a key chooses the sound for the editor: the wave of its file shows where it is. Move Volume or Pan while it plays.</li><li>On <b>Main</b>, push memory 2 (Storm) up, start effect 1 (Lightning) on the <b>Effects</b> view, and press the key of sound 4 (Thunder), then 5 (Far thunder).</li><li><b>Mute</b> in the SOUND section silences every sound at once and blinks while it does. The fader under it is the volume of all sounds, up to 200 %; a double click puts it back to 100 %.</li><li>For a row of sound faders on Main, choose it in <b>Settings</b>. The device the sounds play on, and a second one to listen on, are chosen on the <b>Sounds</b> view.</li></ol>",
